Project Manager Coordinator (Hybrid Onsite)
Location: Nashville, TN
Duration: 6 Months
Interview: Virtual
Work Arrangement: Hybrid Onsite – Local Candidates Only

Job Description
We are seeking an organized and detail-oriented Project Manager Coordinator to support the PMO, including two Senior Project Managers and the PMO Director.
The candidate will assist with project planning, coordination, documentation, tracking, reporting, and stakeholder communication to ensure successful project delivery.

Key Responsibilities
Support Project Managers with daily project coordination.
Maintain project schedules, milestones, and deliverable trackers.
Coordinate meetings, prepare agendas, and document meeting minutes.
Track action items, risks, issues, and project dependencies.
Maintain project plans, status reports, RAID logs, and documentation.
Prepare project dashboards, presentations, and status updates.
Coordinate with cross-functional teams, stakeholders, and vendors.
Support Agile/Scrum ceremonies and project governance activities.
Assist with SharePoint, calendars, onboarding, timesheets, and vendor coordination.

Required Qualifications
Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.
Experience in project coordination, administrative support, operations, or business analysis.
Excellent written and verbal communication skills.
Ability to manage multiple tasks and competing deadlines.
Proficiency in Microsoft Office, including Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams, and SharePoint.
Ability to handle confidential information professionally.

Preferred Qualifications
Knowledge of project management fundamentals and PMO processes.
Familiarity with Agile/Scrum methodologies.
Experience with Planview, Airtable, Microsoft Planner, Jira, Azure DevOps, or SharePoint.
CAPM, Scrum certification, or relevant project management training is a plus.
Core Skills
Project Coordination, PMO Support, Project Documentation, Scheduling, Status Reporting, Risk & Issue Tracking, Stakeholder Management, Microsoft Office, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams, SharePoint, Agile, Scrum, Communication, Organization, Time Management.

